C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Eligibility: All Countries\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>\\u003Cstrong>Deadline: \\u003C\\u002Fstrong>June 30, 2026\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003C\\u002Ful>\\u003Cp>\\u003Cstrong>Bond University Vice Chancellor Scholarship Benefits\\u003C\\u002Fstrong>\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cul>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>As a Vice Chancellor’s Elite Scholar you will be provided with 100% tuition remission for any single or approved combined undergraduate degree.\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>As a Vice Chancellor’s Elite Scholar, you will also be invited to participate in the Vice Chancellor’s Mentoring Program once you commence at Bond.\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>The Mentoring Program connects each scholar with an influential corporate mentor, and is intended to cultivate industry links, networks and business acumen.\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>As a Vice Chancellor’s Elite Scholar, you must commence in the January semester of the year following completion of Year 12, and unfortunately, will not be permitted to defer to a later semester. \\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003C\\u002Ful>\\u003Cp>\\u003Cstrong>Bond University Scholarship Requirements\\u003C\\u002Fstrong>\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cp>To be eligible for the undergraduate Bond University Scholarship, applicants must satisfy the following conditions:\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cul>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Be a domestic student completing Year 12 at an Australian secondary school.\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Be predicted to achieve a minimum of ATAR 95.00 or IB Diploma 38.\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Hold a demonstrated record of leadership, initiative, and service to your school and\\u002For community.  \\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Be prepared to maintain the level of academic and personal excellence that distinguished you as an applicant once you have commenced at Bond. \\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003C\\u002Ful>\\u003Cp>\\u003Cstrong>How To Apply for Bond University Vice Chancellor Scholarship\\u003C\\u002Fstrong>\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cp>To apply for the Bond University Vice Chancellor Scholarship, follow the instructions we have outlined below; \\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cul>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Read all the details provided on this page\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Ensure your eligibility and gather your documents\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Complete the \\u003Ca href=\\\"https:\\u002F\\u002Fstudent-bond.studylink.com\\u002F\\\">Bond University Study Application Form\\u003C\\u002Fa> to lodge your application for your chosen program. \\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Complete the \\u003Ca href=\\\"https:\\u002F\\u002Fstudent-bond.studylink.com\\u002F\\\">Bond University Scholarship Application Form.\\u003C\\u002Fa> Simply use the same log-in details as used for your study application and enter ‘scholarship’ in the keyword field on the ‘Start an Application’ tab. \\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>You must complete and submit your scholarship application before the application closing date as no late scholarship applications will be considered! \\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Click on the button below to begin your application.\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003C\\u002Ful>\\u003Cp>Apply here: \\u003Ca href=\\\"https:\\u002F\\u002Fbond.edu.au\\u002Fscholarship\\u002Fvice-chancellors-elite-scholarship\\\">https:\\u002F\\u002Fbond.edu.au\\u002Fscholarship\\u002Fvice-chancellors-elite-scholarship\\u003C\\u002Fa>\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cp>\\u003C\\u002Fp>\",\"2026-06-15 15:47:08\",[180],{\"fileName\":181,\"oldFileName\":181,\"type\":47,\"file\":48,\"url\":182},\"assets\\u002Felearning\\u002Flrm\\u002Fexplore\\u002Fnews\\u002F2026-bond-university-vice-chancellor-scholarship-how-to-apply\\u002F6a30106c87bff6.51533030_screenshot 2026-06-15 154031.png\",\"https:\\u002F\\u002Flinkskool.com\\u002Fassets\\u002Felearning\\u002Flrm\\u002Fexplore\\u002Fnews\\u002F2026-bond-university-vice-chancellor-scholarship-how-to-apply\\u002F6a30106c87bff6.51533030_screenshot%202026-06-15%20154031.png\",{\"id\":22,\"slug\":184,\"title\":185,\"content\":186,\"authorName\":66,\"authorId\":39,\"status\":40,\"recommended\":41,\"datePosted\":187,\"deadline\":43,\"images\":188,\"notifiedAt\":43,\"notifiedBy\":43,\"createdAt\":187,\"updatedAt\":81,\"readTime\":50},\"2026-qatar-energy-lng-field-operator-program-for-nigerians-career-opportunities-for-nigerians-289\",\"2026 Qatar Energy Lng Field Operator Program For Nigerians: Career Opportunities For Nigerians\",\"\\u003Cp>Qatar Energy LNG is seeking applications from talented professionals from Nigeria for exciting upcoming opportunities to support its operations in Qatar.\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cp>Register your interest today for a chance to join our diverse community of experts.\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cp>\\u003Cstrong>Qatar Energy LNG Field Operator Program Abstract\\u003C\\u002Fstrong>\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cul>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Host: Qatar Energy LNG\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Study Abroad: \\u003Ca href=\\\"https:\\u002F\\u002Fscholarsworld.ng\\u002Fscholarship\\u002F?utm_source=Google&amp;utm_medium=Catergory&amp;utm_campaign=Email+Campaign\\\">Study Abroad\\u003C\\u002Fa> || \\u003Ca href=\\\"https:\\u002F\\u002Fscholarsworld.ng\\u002Fcategory\\u002Fscholarship\\u002Fscholarships-in-asia\\u002F\\\">Study-In-Asia\\u003C\\u002Fa>\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Location: Qatar\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Category: \\u003Ca href=\\\"https:\\u002F\\u002Fscholarsworld.ng\\u002Fscholarships\\u002Finternships\\u002F?utm_source=Google&amp;utm_medium=Catergory&amp;utm_campaign=Email+Campaign\\\">Internships\\u003C\\u002Fa> || \\u003Ca href=\\\"https:\\u002F\\u002Fscholarsworld.ng\\u002Ftrainings\\u002F?utm_source=Google&amp;utm_medium=Catergory&amp;utm_campaign=Email+Campaign\\\">Trainings\\u003C\\u002Fa>\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Benefits:\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cul>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Tax Free Salary\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Housing\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Health Care Insurance\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Family Support\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003C\\u002Ful>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Eligibility: Nigeria\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Deadline: Not Specified\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003C\\u002Ful>\\u003Cp>\\u003Cstrong>Qatar Energy LNG Field Operator Program Details\\u003C\\u002Fstrong>\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cp>Qatar Energy LNG is seeking applications from talented professionals from Nigeria for exciting upcoming opportunities to support its operations in Qatar.\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cp>At QatarEnergy LNG, you will not only build a career with one of the world’s leading LNG companies, but also enjoy a competitive package that includes tax-free salary, housing, healthcare, and family support.\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cp>The recruitment drive specifically targets seasoned operations experts with backgrounds in Utility, Inlet Receiving, Sulphur Recovery, or LNG facilities for full-time employment in the oil and gas sector\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cp>\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cp>\\u003Cstrong>Qatar Energy LNG Field Operator Program 2026 Benefits\\u003C\\u002Fstrong>\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cp>The Qatar Energy LNG Field Operator Program offers the following benefits;\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cul>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Career Opportunity\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Tax-free base salary\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Company-provided housing\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Comprehensive healthcare coverage\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Family support and relocation benefits\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003C\\u002Ful>\\u003Cul>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Maintain the competency of all operational procedures and practices through on-the-job training and job rotation to ensure readiness and capability to assume the operator role.\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Operate field equipment in accordance with operating and approved safety procedures to ensure effective process flows and optimum operational status of equipment.\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Monitor and log all operating parameters ensuring that all irregularities are reported to immediate supervisor for advice and\\u002For resolution.  \\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Prepare field equipment in allocated work area for maintenance activities and follow-up execution and recommission equipment upon satisfactory completion of work.\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Ensure all Permit to Work requirements and expectations throughout Permit to Work issuance in the field and during PTW field audits.\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Monitor all personnel and activities on site using, but limited to, unit surveillance, regular safety walks, audits and Observation Cards to ensure site safety and operational effectiveness.\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Provide immediate first-line response capability in the event of emergencies or major incidents to eliminate or limit potential loss or damage to Company personnel, assets or the environment.\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Ensure incoming shift operator is fully briefed on current operating status and significant events during previous shift to ensure seamless hand-over of responsibilities.\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Collect all regular and special samples correctly as per schedule and direction of shift supervisor.\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u