rships\\u003C\\u002Fa> ||  \\u003Ca href=\\\"https:\\u002F\\u002Fscholarsworld.ng\\u002Fscholarships\\u002Fpostgraduate-scholarships\\u002F?utm_source=Google&amp;utm_medium=Catergory&amp;utm_campaign=Email+Campaign\\\">Postgraduate Scholarships\\u003C\\u002Fa> || \\u003Ca href=\\\"https:\\u002F\\u002Fscholarsworld.ng\\u002Fscholarships\\u002Fmasters-scholarships\\u002F?utm_source=Google&amp;utm_medium=Catergory&amp;utm_campaign=Email+Campaign\\\">Masters Scholarships\\u003C\\u002Fa> || \\u003Ca href=\\\"https:\\u002F\\u002Fscholarsworld.ng\\u002Fscholarships\\u002Fphd-scholarships\\u002F?utm_source=Google&amp;utm_medium=Catergory&amp;utm_campaign=Email+Campaign\\\">PhD Scholarships\\u003C\\u002Fa> \\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Benefits: Full Scholarship\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cul>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Tuition\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Monthly Living Stipends\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Ecocheques\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Internet-Connectivity Allowance\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>A Bicycle Allowance\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>A Full Reimbursement of Public Transport Costs\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003C\\u002Ful>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Eligibility: All Countries\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Deadline: June 25, 2026\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003C\\u002Ful>\\u003Cp>\\u003Cstrong>University of Antwerp Postgraduate Scholarship 2026 Benefits\\u003C\\u002Fstrong>\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cp>The University of Antwerp Postgraduate Scholarship offers the following benefits;\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cul>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp> a doctoral scholarship for a period of two years. Following a positive evaluation, the scholarship can be renewed once for another two-year period.\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Your monthly scholarship amount is calculated according to the \\u003Ca href=\\\"https:\\u002F\\u002Fwww.uantwerpen.be\\u002Fen\\u002Fjobs\\u002Fwhat-do-we-offer\\u002Fsalaries\\u002F\\\">scholarship amounts \\u003C\\u002Fa>for doctoral scholarship holders on the pay scales for contract research staff (Dutch: \\u003Cem>Bijzonder Academisch Personeel\\u003C\\u002Fem>, BAP).\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>As a doctoral researcher, you will have access to a wide and varied range of courses and an \\u003Ca class=\\\"google-anno\\\" href=\\\"https:\\u002F\\u002Fscholarsworld.ng\\u002Funiversity-of-antwerp-postgraduate-scholarship\\u002F#\\\"> \\u003Cu>educational\\u003C\\u002Fu>\\u003C\\u002Fa> credit through the Antwerp Doctoral School.\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>You will receive ecocheques, Internet-connectivity allowance, and a bicycle allowance or a full reimbursement of public transport costs for commuting.\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>You will do most of your work at the City Campus in a dynamic and stimulating working environment.\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003C\\u002Ful>\\u003Cp>\\u003Cstrong>University of Antwerp Scholarship Requirements\\u003C\\u002Fstrong>\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cp>To be eligible for the University of Antwerp Scholarship, applicants must satisfy the following conditions:\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cul>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>You hold a law degree, a master’s degree in law or in social \\u003Ca class=\\\"google-anno\\\" href=\\\"https:\\u002F\\u002Fscholarsworld.ng\\u002Funiversity-of-antwerp-postgraduate-scholarship\\u002F#\\\"> \\u003Cu>sciences\\u003C\\u002Fu>\\u003C\\u002Fa> – in the latter case, with a demonstrated knowledge of and interest in human rights law (or you will have obtained it by the time you start work).\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>You submit a concise research proposal in English for the research you will be developing (see above). This focused proposal of 2 pages includes the following headings: problem statement, central research question, methodology and core bibliography. You pay attention to global justice and Global South dimensions. The proposal should allow you to successfully complete the PhD in 4 years.\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>You can demonstrate excellent study results, in particular in the broad area of human rights law. You substantiate this with a detailed overview of your study results (see ‘Want to apply?’).\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>You have an adequate command of English or Dutch to be able to provide teaching (support).\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003C\\u002Ful>\\u003Cul>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Your teaching competences are in line with the University of Antwerp’s \\u003Ca href=\\\"https:\\u002F\\u002Fwww.uantwerpen.be\\u002Fen\\u002Fabout-uantwerp\\u002Forganisation\\u002Fmission-and-vision\\u002Fthree-core-tasks\\u002Feducation\\u002F\\\">educational vision\\u003C\\u002Fa>.\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Your research qualities are in line with the faculty and \\u003Ca href=\\\"https:\\u002F\\u002Fwww.uantwerpen.be\\u002Fen\\u002Fresearch\\u002Fmanagement\\u002F\\\">university research policies\\u003C\\u002Fa>.\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>You are willing to apply for (additional) research funding.\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>You have a particular interest in scientific research in the field of hum\\u003Cstrong>an rights law and global justice.\\u003C\\u002Fstrong>\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>\\u003Cstrong>You combine a deep knowledge of the human rights law with a research interest in the global (South) context.\\u003C\\u002Fstrong>\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003C\\u002Ful>\\u003Cp>University of Antwerp Scholarship 2026 Required Documents\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cp>While applying for the University of Antwerp Faculty of Law Scholarship 2026, you will be required to submit the following documents;\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cul>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>a motivation letter\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>a concise research proposal of 2 pages for the research you will be developing (see above)\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>a detailed overview of your study grades\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>your (academic) CV\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003C\\u002Ful>\\u003Cp>\\u003Cstrong>How To Apply for University of Antwerp Postgraduate Scholarship\\u003C\\u002Fstrong>\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cp>To apply for the University of Antwerp Postgraduate Scholarship 2026, follow the instructions we have outlined below; \\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cul>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Read the information we have provided on this webpage and ensure your eligibility\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Apply through the University of Antwerp’s online job application platform\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003C\\u002Ful>\\u003Cp>\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cp>APPLY HERE: \\u003Ca href=\\\"https:\\u002F\\u002Fwww.uantwerpen.be\\u002Fen\\u002Fjobs\\u002Fvacancies\\u002Facademic-staff\\u002F?q=4429&amp;descr=Doctoral-scholarship-holder-in-the-broad-field-of-human-rights-law-and-global-justice\\\">https:\\u002F\\u002Fwww.uantwerpen.be\\u002Fen\\u002Fjobs\\u002Fvacancies\\u002Facademic-staff\\u002F?q=4429&amp;descr=Doctoral-scholarship-holder-in-the-broad-field-of-human-rights-law-and-global-justice\\u003C\\u002Fa>\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cp>\\u003C\\u002Fp>\",\"2026-06-08 12:07:16\",[216],{\"fileName\":217,\"oldFileName\":217,\"type\":47,\"file\":48,\"url\":218},\"assets\\u002Felearning\\u002Flrm\\u002Fexplore\\u002Fnews\\u002F2026-university-of-antwerp-postgraduate-scholarship-in-human-rights-law-and-global-justice-fully-funded-in-belgium\\u002F6a26a2648ec477.99908277_screenshot 2026-06-08 115733.png\",\"https:\\u002F\\u002Flinkskool.com\\u002Fassets\\u002Felearning\\u002Flrm\\u002Fexplore\\u002Fnews\\u002F2026-university-of-antwerp-postgraduate-scholarship-in-human-rights-law-and-global-justice-fully-funded-in-belgium\\u002F6a26a2648ec477.99908277_screenshot%202026-06-08%20115733.png\",{\"id\":26,\"slug\":220,\"title\":221,\"content\":222,\"authorName\":66,\"authorId\":39,\"status\":40,\"recommended\":41,\"datePosted\":223,\"deadline\":43,\"images\":224,\"notifiedAt\":43,\"notifiedBy\":43,\"createdAt\":223,\"updatedAt\":81,\"readTime\":61},\"simmons-university-undergraduate-scholarship-2026-fully-funded-opportunity-285\",\"Simmons University Undergraduate Scholarship 2026: Fully Funded Opportunity\",\"\\u003Cp>The Simmons University Distinguished Scholar Award will cover the full tuition, housing, fees, plus an additional $3,000 for academic pursuits such as study abroad, research support, and more.\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cp>Simmons University, located in the Fenway district of Boston, is a co-ed university that focuses on women’s \\u003Ca class=\\\"google-anno\\\" href=\\\"https:\\u002F\\u002Fscholarsworld.ng\\u002Fsimmons-university-undergraduate-scholarship\\u002F#\\\"> \\u003Cu>education\\u003C\\u002Fu>\\u003C\\u002Fa> at the undergraduate level.\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cp>\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cp>\\u003Cstrong>Simmons University Distinguished Scholar Award Abstract\\u003C\\u002Fstrong>\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cul>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Scholarship Host: Simmons University\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Category: \\u003Ca href=\\\"https:\\u002F\\u002Fscholarsworld.ng\\u002Fscholarships\\u002F\\\">Scholarships\\u003C\\u002Fa> | \\u003Ca href=\\\"https:\\u002F\\u002Fscholarsworld.ng\\u002Fscholarship\\u002F\\\">Study Abroad \\u003C\\u002Fa>| \\u003Ca href=\\\"https:\\u002F\\u002Fscholarsworld.ng\\u002Fscholarships\\u002Fundergraduate-scholarships\\u002F\\\">Undergraduate Scholarships\\u003C\\u002Fa>\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Benefits: Full Scholarship\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cul>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Tuition fees\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>$3,000 Living Stipends\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Accommodation\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003C\\u002Ful>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Eligibility: All Countries\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Deadline: December 1. Yearly\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003C\\u002Ful>\\u003Cp>\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cp>\\u003Cstrong>Simmons University Undergraduate Scholarship Details\\u003C\\u002Fstrong>\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cp>The Kotzen undergraduate scholarship at Simmons is the most prestigious award offered at Simmons and acknowledges excellence through a focus on study abroad, scholarly research, and intellectual curiosity.\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cp>\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cp>\\u003Cstrong>Simmons University Undergraduate Scholarship Requirements\\u003C\\u002Fstrong>\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cp>Students applying for the Simmons University Undergraduate Scholarship must meet the following criteria:\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cul>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Apply as a first-year for the fall semester\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Simmons is test-optional, so it is your choice if you would like to submit standardized test scores with your admission application. For those choosing to submit test scores, a 28 or higher on the ACT is recommended, and a 1300 or higher on the SAT\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Non-native English speakers must submit an English proficiency test (TOEFL\\u002FIELTS, TOEFL Essentials, SAT\\u002FACT scores, or Duolingo English Test)\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>GPA of 3.3 or higher, unweighted\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>College preparatory curriculum including an advanced level math course during, or prior to, your senior year of high school\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>A record of taking honors, advanced placement (AP), and international baccalaureate (IB) courses, as available in their high school systems\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003C\\u002Ful>\\u003Cp>\\u003Cstrong>Simmons University Undergraduate Scholarship Benefits and Timeline\\u003C\\u002Fstrong>\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cul>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>The Kotzen Scholarship provides full tuition, room &amp; board, plus an additional $3,000 for academic pursuits such as study abroad, research support, and more.\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>This scholarship is awarded for the duration of a four-year period of full-time undergraduate study and supersedes any previously awarded merit scholarship. \\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003C\\u002Ful>\\u003Cp>\\u003Cstrong>Required Documents for Kotzen Undergraduate Scholarship\\u003C\\u002Fstrong>\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cul>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Academic Transcripts\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Record of Honors\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>ACT\\u002FSAT Scores (Optional)\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>English Proficiency Test\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Recommendation Letters\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003C\\u002Ful>\\u003Cp>\\u003Cstrong>Simmons University Undergraduate Scholarship Details\\u003C\\u002Fstrong>\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cp>The Kotzen undergraduate scholarship at Simmons is the most prestigious award offered at Simmons and acknowledges excellence through a focus on study abroad, scholarly research, and intellectual curiosity.\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cp>\\u003Cstrong>Simmons University Undergraduate Scholarship Requirements\\u003C\\u002Fstrong>\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cp>Students applying for the Simmons University Undergraduate Scholarship must meet the following criteria:\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cul>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Apply as a first-year for the fall semester\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Simmons is test-optional, so it is your choice if you would like to submit standardized test scores with your admission application. For those choosing to submit test scores, a 28 or higher on the ACT is recommended, and a 1300 or higher on the SAT\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Non-native English speakers must submit an English proficiency test (TOEFL\\u002FIELTS, TOEFL Essentials, SAT\\u002FACT scores, or Duolingo English Test)\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>GPA of 3.3 or higher, unweighted\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>College preparatory curriculum including an advanced level math course during, or prior to, your senior year of high school\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>A record of taking honors, advanced placement (AP), and international baccalaureate (IB) courses, as available in their high school systems\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003C\\u002Ful>\\u003Cp>\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cp>How To Apply for 2026 Simmons University Undergraduate Scholarship in USA\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cul>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>The application consists of a short answer and a formal essay in response to the prompts below, as well as a resume including activities and involvements.\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Students should submit their essays and resume in \\u003Cstrong>PDF\\u003C\\u002Fstrong> or \\u003Cstrong>Word Doc\\u003C\\u002Fstrong> \\u003Ca href=\\\"mailto:ugadm@simmons.edu\\\">via email\\u003C\\u002Fa> with the subject line “Kotzen Application,” by December 1. Each page of the document should include the student’s full name and date of birth.\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003C\\u002Ful>\\u003Cul>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Please note: it is the student’s responsibility to submit a working file in the proper format (PDF or Word), as we will not convert or accept incompatible files (i.e., Google Docs, Pages, etc.)\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003C\\u002Ful>\\u003Cp>Short Answer \\u003Cem>(of no more than 250 words)\\u003C\\u002Fem>: How would you use your additional annual award of $3,000 (for study abroad, short-term courses, summer internship tuition, and\\u002For research support)?\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cul>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Formal Essay \\u003Cem>(of no more than 500 words)\\u003C\\u002Fem>: Some people argue that leaders are born, not made, while others defend the opposite view, namely that leaders are “made.” Write an essay in which you defend one view or the other. Use a specific example of a leader, either from history or from your own personal experience, to support your argument.\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003C\\u002Ful>\\u003Cp>\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cp>APPLY HERE: \\u003Ca href=\\\"https:\\u002F\\u002Fwww.simmons.edu\\u002Fundergraduate\\u002Fadmission-and-financial-aid\\u002Ftuition-financial-aid\\u002Ftypes-financial-aid\\u002Fscholarships\\u002Fdistinguished-scholar\\\">https:\\u002F\\u002Fwww.simmons.edu\\u002Fundergraduate\\u002Fadmission-and-financial-aid\\u002Ftuition-financial-aid\\u002Ftypes-financial-aid\\u002Fscholarships\\u002Fdistinguished-scholar\\u003C\\u002Fa>\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cp>\\u003C\\u002Fp>\",\"2026-06-08 11:52:38\",[225],{\"fileName\":226,\"oldFileName\":226,\"type\":47,\"file\":48,\"url\":227},\"assets\\u002Felearning\\u002Flrm\\u002Fexplore\\u002Fnews\\u002Fsimmons-university-undergraduate-scholarship-2026-fully-funded-opportunity\\u002F6a269ef664b645.15836393_screenshot 2026-06-08 114512.png\",\"https:\\u002F\\u002Flinkskool.com\\u002Fassets\\u002Felearning\\u002Flrm\\u002Fexplore\\u002Fnews\\u002Fsimmons-university-undergraduate-scholarship-2026-fully-funded-opportunity\\u002F6a269ef664b645.15836393_screenshot%202026-06-08%20114512.png\",{\"id\":27,\"slug\":229,\"title\":230,\"content\":231,\"authorName\":66,\"authorId\":39,\"status\":40,\"recommended\":41,\"datePosted\":232,\"deadline\":43,\"images\":233,\"notifiedAt\":43,\"notifiedBy\":43,\"createdAt\":232,\"updatedAt\":81,\"readTime\":50},\"boston-college-gabelli-presidential-scholarship-2026-in-usa-fully-funded-opportunity-284\",\"Boston College Gabelli Presidential Scholarship 2026 In Usa | Fully Funded Opportunity\",\"\\u003Cp>The Boston College Gabelli Presidential Scholarship covers the full tuition at BC, for all successful domestic and international applicants interested in studying in the United States of America. \\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cp>Irrespective of the financial needs of the student, the Boston College Gabelli Presidential Scholarship will cover the full cost of tuition as students are automatically reviewed for the scholarship when they apply.\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cp>The Gabelli Presidential Scholars Program works in tandem with the University’s rigorous curricula, challenging Scholars over four years through summer programs focusing on service learning, international experience, and professional internships.\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cp>\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cp>\\u003Cstrong>Boston College Gabelli Presidential Scholarship Abstract\\u003C\\u002Fstrong>\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cul>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Scholarship Host: Boston College\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Category: \\u003Ca href=\\\"https:\\u002F\\u002Fscholarsworld.ng\\u002Fscholarships\\u002F\\\">Scholarships\\u003C\\u002Fa> || \\u003Ca href=\\\"https:\\u002F\\u002Fscholarsworld.ng\\u002Fscholarship\\u002F\\\">Study Abroad\\u003C\\u002Fa> || \\u003Ca href=\\\"https:\\u002F\\u002Fscholarsworld.ng\\u002Fscholarships\\u002Fundergraduate-scholarships\\u002F\\\">Undergraduate Scholarships\\u003C\\u002Fa>\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Benefits: Full Scholarship\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Eligibility: All Countries\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Deadline: November 1, Yearly \\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003C\\u002Ful>\\u003Cp>\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cp>\\u003Cstrong>Boston College Gabelli Presidential Scholarship Details\\u003C\\u002Fstrong>\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cp>The Gabelli Presidential Scholars Program is an undergraduate academic merit program that annually awards full-tuition scholarships and fully-funded, GPSP-sponsored summer programs to 18 incoming freshman students.\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cp>Early Decision and Regular Decision applicants who submit their BC applications by the November 1 priority scholarship deadline will be considered.  There is no separate application for this scholarship, but please note that only candidates for \\u003Cstrong>fall\\u003C\\u002Fstrong> \\u003Cstrong>admission\\u003C\\u002Fstrong> will be considered. Presently, there are 60 Scholars in the program.\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cp>The Gabelli Presidential Scholars Program works in tandem with the University’s rigorous curricula, challenging Scholars over four years through summer programs focusing on service learning, international experience, and professional internships. During the academic year, Scholars interact with one another on a weekly basis.\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cp>\\u003Cstrong>Boston College Gabelli Presidential Scholarship Requirements\\u003C\\u002Fstrong>\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cp>The requirements for the consideration of the Boston College Gabelli Presidential Scholarship include the following;\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cul>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Applicant must apply for admission into BC by the priority scholarship deadline of November 1.\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>No separate application is required for the Boston College Gabelli Presidential Scholarship, and you may apply as an Early Decision I, Early Decision II or as a Regular Decision applicant.\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>All applicants who apply by the deadline are automatically considered for the Scholarship. \\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>The scholarship does not have a minimum GPA or SAT score requirement. However, students with outstanding academic records, who hold leadership roles in their school and who are committed to and have a demonstrated interest in community service, are usually given priority consideration.\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003C\\u002Ful>\\u003Cp>\\u003Cstrong>Gabelli Presidential Scholarship Benefits and Timeline\\u003C\\u002Fstrong>\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cp>The Boston University Gabelli Presidential Scholarship will cover the full tuition of selected candidates, regardless of financial need, and therefore does not require any financial aid forms to be submitted. \\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cp>The Presidential Scholarship will be retained for scholars to remain in the program for their 4 years at BC provided they maintain a 3.5 GPA and remain model citizens of the BC community throughout that time. \\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cp>\\u003Cstrong>How To Apply for Gabelli Presidential Scholarship\\u003C\\u002Fstrong>\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cul>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>There is no separate application for this scholarship, applicants are only required to apply for admission into any of the accreditted programs at Boston College.\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Please note that only candidates for \\u003Cstrong>fall\\u003C\\u002Fstrong> \\u003Cstrong>admission\\u003C\\u002Fstrong> will be considered.\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Don’t miss out on this remarkable opportunity to pave your path to \\u003Ca class=\\\"google-anno\\\" href=\\\"https:\\u002F\\u002Fscholarsworld.ng\\u002Fboston-college-gabelli-presidential-scholarship\\u002F#\\\"> \\u003Cu>educational\\u003C\\u002Fu>\\u003C\\u002Fa> excellence. Apply today and set the course for academic success!\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Click on the button below to begin your application and read more about the scholarship\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003C\\u002Ful>\\u003Cp>APPLY HERE: \\u003Ca href=\\\"https:\\u002F\\u002Fwww.bc.edu\\u002Fcontent\\u002Fbc-web\\u002Fadmission.html\\\">https:\\u002F\\u002Fwww.bc.edu\\u002Fcontent\\u002Fbc-web\\u002Fadmission.html\\u003C\\u002Fa>\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cp>\\u003C\\u002Fp>\",\"2026-06-08 11:43:25\",[234],{\"fileName\":235,\"oldFileName\":235,\"type\":47,\"file\":48,\"url\":2