Study Abroad\\u003C\\u002Fa> || \\u003Ca href=\\\"https:\\u002F\\u002Fscholarsworld.ng\\u002Fcategory\\u002Fscholarship\\u002Fscholarships-in-usa\\u002F?utm_source=Google&amp;utm_medium=Catergory&amp;utm_campaign=Email+Campaign\\\">Study-In-USA\\u003C\\u002Fa>\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Location: USA\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Category: \\u003Ca href=\\\"https:\\u002F\\u002Fscholarsworld.ng\\u002Fscholarships\\u002F?utm_source=Google&amp;utm_medium=Catergory&amp;utm_campaign=Email+Campaign\\\">Scholarships\\u003C\\u002Fa> ||  \\u003Ca href=\\\"https:\\u002F\\u002Fscholarsworld.ng\\u002Fscholarships\\u002Fpostgraduate-scholarships\\u002F?utm_source=Google&amp;utm_medium=Catergory&amp;utm_campaign=Email+Campaign\\\">Postgraduate Scholarships\\u003C\\u002Fa> || \\u003Ca href=\\\"https:\\u002F\\u002Fscholarsworld.ng\\u002Fscholarships\\u002Fmasters-scholarships\\u002F?utm_source=Google&amp;utm_medium=Catergory&amp;utm_campaign=Email+Campaign\\\">Masters Scholarships\\u003C\\u002Fa> || \\u003Ca href=\\\"https:\\u002F\\u002Fscholarsworld.ng\\u002Fscholarships\\u002Fphd-scholarships\\u002F?utm_source=Google&amp;utm_medium=Catergory&amp;utm_campaign=Email+Campaign\\\">PhD Scholarships\\u003C\\u002Fa> \\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Benefits: Full Scholarship\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cul>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Tuition\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>$31,333 Living Stipends\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Medical Insurance\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003C\\u002Ful>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Eligibility: All Countries\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Deadline: June 30, 2026\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003C\\u002Ful>\\u003Cp>\\u003Cstrong>University of Maine Scholarship 2026 Benefits\\u003C\\u002Fstrong>\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cul>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>This position provides 2 years of funding for MSc and 3 years for PhD candidates, comprising a 20-hour-per-week assistantship with an annual stipend of $28,000 (MS) or 31,333 (PhD).\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>The University of Maine will cover 65% of health insurance costs and 50% dental insurance costs.\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Additional benefits include office space, operational support (including laptop access and travel funds), and an out-of-state tuition waiver.\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003C\\u002Ful>\\u003Cp>\\u003Cstrong>Responsibilities of the Graduate Assistant\\u003C\\u002Fstrong>\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cp>The Graduate Assistant will be responsible for:\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cul>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>developing quantitative economic analyses and applying ecological models to assess forest responses to management practices\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>analyzing long-term inventory plot data and Forest Inventory and Analysis (FIA) data\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>communicating research findings to stakeholders, industry partners, and state-level policymakers.\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>The position also involves contributing to peer-reviewed publications and technical reports.\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>The student will work closely with an interdisciplinary team at the University of Maine and various key partners in forestry sector in the Northeast US.\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003C\\u002Ful>\\u003Cp>\\u003Cstrong>University of Maine Scholarship Requirements\\u003C\\u002Fstrong>\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cp>To be eligible for the  postgraduate University of Maine Scholarship, applicants must satisfy the following conditions\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cul>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>hold a B.S. degree in Forestry, Economics, Statistics, or a quantitatively focused Environmental or Social \\u003Ca class=\\\"google-anno\\\" href=\\\"https:\\u002F\\u002Fscholarsworld.ng\\u002Funiversity-of-maine-scholarship\\u002F#\\\"> \\u003Cu>Science\\u003C\\u002Fu>\\u003C\\u002Fa> discipline, with a background in natural resource management.\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>have a high GPA, strong GRE scores, and solid \\u003Ca class=\\\"google-anno\\\" href=\\\"https:\\u002F\\u002Fscholarsworld.ng\\u002Funiversity-of-maine-scholarship\\u002F#\\\"> \\u003Cu>scientific\\u003C\\u002Fu>\\u003C\\u002Fa> writing and communication skills.\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>have experience with statistical analysis, GIS, and programming.\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003C\\u002Ful>\\u003Cul>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>The ideal candidate will demonstrate proficiency in quantitative analysis, an ability to work independently, a research interest, and a record of scholastic achievement.\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Women and minorities are strongly encouraged to apply.\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003C\\u002Ful>\\u003Cp>University of Maine Scholarship 2026 Required Documents\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cp>While applying for the University of Maine Scholarship 2026, you will be required to submit the following documents;\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cul>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>A cover letter explaining your interest in the position, your qualifications, and how your interests and skills align with this research project\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>A CV that includes contact information for three references\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>University Transcripts\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>GRE scores\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003C\\u002Ful>\\u003Cp>\\u003Cstrong>How To Apply for University of Maine Scholarship 2026\\u003C\\u002Fstrong>\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cp>To apply for the University of Maine Graduate Assistantship 2026, follow the instructions we have outlined below; \\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cul>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Read the information we have provided on this webpage and ensure your eligibility\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Prepare the required documents\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Please submit a cover letter explaining your interest in the position, your qualifications, and how your interests and skills align with this research project, a CV that includes contact information for three references, university transcripts, and GRE scores (if available) via this \\u003Ca href=\\\"https:\\u002F\\u002Fforms.gle\\u002Fr5Dr49vP6Ab3q1hc7\\\">google form\\u003C\\u002Fa>.\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>For more details, please contact:\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cul>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Dr. Libin T. Louis\\u003Cbr \\u002F>Assistant Professor of Forestry, University of Maine at Fort Kent\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003Cli>\\u003Cp>Graduate Faculty, University of Maine, Orono Email: \\u003Ca href=\\\"mailto:Libin.louis@maine.edu\\\">Libin.louis@maine.edu\\u003C\\u002Fa> \\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003C\\u002Ful>\\u003C\\u002Fli>\\u003C\\u002Ful>\\u003Cp>Apply here: \\u003Ca href=\\\"https:\\u002F\\u002Fdocs.google.com\\u002Fforms\\u002Fd\\u002Fe\\u002F1FAIpQLSf15cDtfYykT_ZJw-mothAk8hRCJFkpJLuw5ceVZB_H2cC6BA\\u002Fviewform\\\">https:\\u002F\\u002Fdocs.google.com\\u002Fforms\\u002Fd\\u002Fe\\u002F1FAIpQLSf15cDtfYykT_ZJw-mothAk8hRCJFkpJLuw5ceVZB_H2cC6BA\\u002Fviewform\\u003C\\u002Fa>\\u003C\\u002Fp>\\u003Cp>\\u003C\\u002Fp>\",\"2026-06-08 11:09:07\",[261],{\"fileName\":262,\"oldFileName\":262,\"type\":47,\"file\":48,\"url\":263},\"assets\\u002Felearning\\u002Flrm\\u002Fexplore\\u002Fnews\\u002Funiversity-of-maine-scholarship-2026-fully-funded-in-usa\\u002F6a2694c3a61f96.22839170_screenshot 2026-06-08 103258.png\",\"https:\\u002F\\u002Flinkskool.com\\u002Fassets\\u002Felearning\\u002Flrm\\u002Fexplore\\u002Fnews\\u002Funiversity-of-maine-scholarship-2026-fully-funded-in-usa\\u002F6a2694c3a61f96.22839170_screenshot%202026-06-08%20103258.png\",{\"id\":31,\"slug\":265,\"title\":266,\"content\":267,\"auth